## Backend Implementation (Status: Tasks/Runs read APIs wired)
As of 2026-02-05, the backend has DB-backed read APIs for Tasks/Runs/Events/Memory links (parameterized SQL; no Alembic churn):
- Schemas:
  - `demo/full-stack-fastapi-template/backend/app/models.py` (`TaskPublic`, `RunPublic`, `RunEventPublic`, `RunDetailPublic`)
- Routes:
  - `demo/full-stack-fastapi-template/backend/app/api/routes/tasks.py`
  - `demo/full-stack-fastapi-template/backend/app/api/routes/runs.py`
- Router registration:
  - `demo/full-stack-fastapi-template/backend/app/api/main.py`

Endpoints (auth required):
- `GET /api/v1/tasks/`
  - `workflow_key` (optional)
  - `status` (optional)
  - `q` (optional; `ILIKE` on `title`, `goal`, `acceptance_criteria`, `workflow_key`)
  - `skip`/`limit`
- `GET /api/v1/tasks/{task_id}`
- `GET /api/v1/tasks/{task_id}/runs`
- `PATCH /api/v1/tasks/{task_id}` (update title; touches `last_touched_at`)
- `GET /api/v1/runs/{run_id}`
- `GET /api/v1/runs/{run_id}/detail` (run + events + memory links with embedded `library_item`)

## Backend Implementation (Status: Library API wired)
As of 2026-02-04 08:55 UTC, the backend has a first-pass `Library` API implemented (read + create + supersede-update):
- Models/schemas:
  - `demo/full-stack-fastapi-template/backend/app/models.py` (`LibraryItem*`)
- Routes:
  - `demo/full-stack-fastapi-template/backend/app/api/routes/library.py`
- Router registration:
  - `demo/full-stack-fastapi-template/backend/app/api/main.py`

Endpoints:
- `GET /api/v1/library/` (auth required)
  - `workflow_key` (optional)
  - `kind` (optional)
  - `q` (optional; `ILIKE` on `title`, `body_mdc`, `workflow_key`, or bucket name)
  - `current_only` (default true; filters `superseded_by_id is null`)
  - `skip`/`limit`
- `GET /api/v1/library/workflow-keys` (auth required)
  - Distinct `workflow_key` values + `bucket_name` + counts (supports bucket grouping UI)
- `GET /api/v1/library/{id}` (auth required)
- `POST /api/v1/library/` (**superuser required**)
- `PUT /api/v1/library/{id}` (**superuser required**)
  - Creates a new row and sets `superseded_by_id` on the old row (never edits content in place)

